---
interface Props {
  kind: 'cloud' | 'leadership';
}
const { kind } = Astro.props;
---

<section class="calculated-chart" aria-label="Example system relationships">
  <h3>
    {kind === 'cloud'
      ? 'The platform boundary and its dependencies.'
      : 'Systems and ownership in the shared alternative.'}
  </h3>
  <div class="dependency-nodes">
    <div data-system="applications">
      <strong>
        {kind === 'cloud'
          ? 'Caller → authenticated gateway'
          : 'Application A + Application B'}
      </strong>
      <small>
        {kind === 'cloud'
          ? 'Identity validation precedes operation authorization.'
          : 'Each application team owns its user workflow.'}
      </small>
    </div>
    <div data-system="interface">
      <strong>
        {kind === 'cloud'
          ? 'Application authorization → service route'
          : 'Shared AI interface'}
      </strong>
      <small>
        {kind === 'cloud'
          ? 'Read is allowed; employee write is denied before routing.'
          : 'The platform team owns the contract and service operation.'}
      </small>
    </div>
    <div data-system="platform">
      <strong>
        {kind === 'cloud'
          ? 'Kubernetes workload boundary'
          : 'Shared model service'}
      </strong>
      <small>
        {kind === 'cloud'
          ? 'Separate application and model-serving workloads; container images define processes.'
          : 'Applications depend on the platform’s availability and supported interface.'}
      </small>
    </div>
    <div data-system="data">
      <strong>Scoped procedure data</strong>
      <small>
        Document owners maintain versions and access rules. The application only
        supplies permitted evidence.
      </small>
    </div>
    {kind === 'cloud' && (
      <div data-system="observability">
        <strong>Observability and operating owner</strong>
        <small>
          Gateway and services emit decision and execution evidence. Define
          incident response and recovery separately.
        </small>
      </div>
    )}
  </div>
  <p class="chart-note">
    Relationships:{' '}
    {kind === 'cloud'
      ? 'caller → gateway → application policy → application service; application → procedure data and model service; gateway and services → observability. Identity controls apply at entry; application policy controls operations; Kubernetes API permissions are separate.'
      : 'application A and application B → shared AI interface → model service; the shared application layer reads scoped procedure data. Ownership boundaries do not remove these dependencies.'}
  </p>
  <p class="chart-note">
    Hypothetical example topology. A container or cluster boundary alone does
    not enforce every data or application permission.
  </p>
</section>
